IMPORT prelude

-- Japan: Act on Promotion of Research and Development, and Utilization of
-- Artificial Intelligence-related Technology (Act No. 53 of 2025)
-- 人工知能関連技術の研究開発及び活用の推進に関する法律（令和七年法律第五十三号）
--
-- THE DOMAIN MODULE: nouns only. Every other module imports it.
-- A DRAFT. Not for use as advice. No domain expert and no lawyer qualified in
-- Japan has read this encoding against the source.
--
-- SEAT: a business operator that develops, provides or uses AI-related
-- technology (the Act's 活用事業者, "utilization business operator", Article 7).
--
-- Two kinds of noun live here.
--   1. Facts the business can state about itself, its technology, a government
--      measure it is asked to cooperate with, and an AI-related incident.
--   2. The vocabulary of the provisions table in jp-ai-articles.l4: one row per
--      provision, recording whom it addresses, the Japanese verb form it uses,
--      what it means for a business operator, and which of the searched-for
--      mechanisms (a reporting duty, a penalty, naming, an investigation or
--      order power, a duty to comply) it carries.

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- 1. Facts the business can state
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

-- Article 2's two limbs, asked as facts about the technology. Whether a given
-- system meets them is a reading of Article 2 (fork F3 in NOTES.md).
DECLARE `The technology` HAS
    `technology necessary for realizing the function of substituting, by artificial means, intellectual abilities relating to human cognition, inference and judgement` IS A BOOLEAN
    `technology relating to an information processing system that processes input information using that technology and outputs the result` IS A BOOLEAN

-- Article 7's description of a utilization business operator, and Article 6(1)'s
-- description of a research and development institute, asked as facts about the
-- business. "Intends to" is the Act's own word (しようとする).
-- The last field is Article 25(1)'s list of addressees, shortened: in full it is
-- the heads of relevant administrative bodies, local governments, incorporated
-- administrative agencies (独立行政法人) and local incorporated administrative
-- agencies (地方独立行政法人), and the representatives of special corporations
-- (特殊法人). "Incorporated administrative agency" in the field name covers both
-- kinds of agency. The name is kept because tests-independent.l4, which this
-- encoding may not edit, uses it.
DECLARE `The business` HAS
    `develops or provides, or intends to develop or provide, products or services that use the technology` IS A BOOLEAN
    `uses, or intends to use, the technology in its business activities` IS A BOOLEAN
    `a university, a research and development corporation, or another institute that researches and develops the technology` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the head of a relevant administrative body, local government or incorporated administrative agency, or the representative of a special corporation` IS A BOOLEAN

-- A government measure or request the business has been asked to cooperate with.
-- Which statutory power it is made under is a fact the business is told, or can
-- find out; it is not something this Act lets the business decide (fork F5).
DECLARE `The measure` HAS
    `implemented by the national government under Article 4` IS A BOOLEAN
    `implemented by a local government under Article 5` IS A BOOLEAN
    `a request for cooperation from the Artificial Intelligence Strategic Headquarters` IS A BOOLEAN

-- An AI-related incident, as Article 16 frames it: a case where citizens' rights
-- and interests are infringed in connection with research and development or
-- utilization of AI-related technology for a wrongful purpose or by an
-- inappropriate method.
DECLARE `The incident` HAS
    `citizens' rights and interests were infringed` IS A BOOLEAN
    `arose from research and development or utilization of the technology for a wrongful purpose` IS A BOOLEAN
    `arose from research and development or utilization of the technology by an inappropriate method` IS A BOOLEAN

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- 2. The vocabulary of the provisions table
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

DECLARE `Part of the Act` IS ONE OF
    `Chapter I, General Provisions`
    `Chapter II, Basic Measures`
    `Chapter III, Artificial Intelligence Basic Plan`
    `Chapter IV, Artificial Intelligence Strategic Headquarters`
    `the Supplementary Provisions`

-- Who the provision speaks to. Officials appear here only as addressees; none
-- of them has a seat.
DECLARE `Addressee` IS ONE OF
    `nobody: a purpose, a definition or a principle`
    `the measures to be taken, in the passive`
    `Japan (我が国)`
    `the national government (国)`
    `local governments (地方公共団体)`
    `the national government and local governments (国及び地方公共団体)`
    `research and development institutes (研究開発機関)`
    `utilization business operators (活用事業者)`
    `citizens (国民)`
    `the Government (政府)`
    `the Headquarters or its officers (本部, 本部長, 副本部長, 本部員)`
    `the Cabinet Office (内閣府)`
    `another Act, by amendment`

-- The verb form, with the Japanese behind it. The English words are the
-- translator's; the Japanese in brackets was read in ai-act-ja.txt.
-- Where two limbs are joined by とともに, the label puts the closing verb on the
-- second limb only (forks F1 for Article 7 and F12 for Article 8 in NOTES.md).
DECLARE `Verb form` IS ONE OF
    `states the purpose (目的とする)`
    `defines a term (をいう)`
    `is to (ものとする)`
    `is to endeavor (努めるものとする)`
    `is to endeavor, and is to endeavor to cooperate (努めるとともに、協力するよう努めるものとする)`
    `deepens, and is to endeavor to cooperate (深めるとともに、協力するよう努めるものとする)`
    `is responsible for (責務を有する)`
    `measures must be taken, in the passive (講じられなければならない)`
    `endeavor, and must give due consideration (努めるとともに、配慮しなければならない)`
    `endeavor, and must cooperate (努めるとともに、協力しなければならない)`
    `may request (求めることができる)`
    `may ask for (依頼することができる)`
    `establishes, constitutes or assigns an organ (置く, 組織する, 充てる, つかさどる, 処理する, とする)`
    `delegates to Cabinet Order (政令で定める)`
    `comes into effect (施行する)`
    `amends another Act (read in the English translation only)`

-- What the provision means for a business operator.
DECLARE `Bearing on a business operator` IS ONE OF
    `none: not addressed to a business operator`
    `the basic principles a business operator acts in accordance with`
    `defines the technology that makes a business a utilization business operator`
    `the measures a business operator must cooperate with`
    `an endeavor, if the business is also a research and development institute`
    `an endeavor, and a duty to cooperate`
    `names business operators as partners in, or users of, a government measure`
    `the national government is to establish guidelines for appropriate research, development and utilization`
    `the national government is to give guidance, advice or information to the business`
    `the Headquarters may ask the business for cooperation`
    `the Headquarters may request cooperation from the representative of a special corporation, which can itself be a business operator`
    `fixes when the provisions take effect`

-- The mechanisms searched for in every provision. A provision's list holds
-- those it carries toward a private person.
DECLARE `Mechanism` IS ONE OF
    `a duty to report an incident or a case to an authority`
    `a penalty, fine or other sanction`
    `publication of a person's name`
    `an investigation, inspection or order addressed to a private person`
    `a duty to comply with a request`

DECLARE `A provision` HAS
    `the provision`                                IS A STRING
    `in the main provisions`                       IS A BOOLEAN
    `the article number`                           IS A NUMBER
    `part`                                         IS A `Part of the Act`
    `addressed to`                                 IS AN `Addressee`
    `the verb form`                                IS A `Verb form`
    `what it means for a business operator`        IS A `Bearing on a business operator`
    `mechanisms affecting a private person`        IS A LIST OF `Mechanism`
